sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant App as Application
    participant Rel as Relational
    participant Doc as Document
    participant Gr as Graph
    App->>Rel: query with joins across normalised tables
    Rel-->>App: one row set, written once, joined many times
    App->>Doc: fetch one self-contained document
    Doc-->>App: the whole tree in one read
    Note over App,Doc: fast when the access pattern matches the nesting — painful when it stops matching
    App->>Gr: traverse relationships several hops out
    Gr-->>App: the path
    Note over App,Gr: the same query in SQL is a pile of self-joins
    Note over App,Rel: the data model is a bet on the access pattern — schema-on-read moves the cost, it does not remove it
